00:20:07.886 --> 00:20:09.270
We also have
our tool, and we then

00:20:09.271 --> 00:20:11.230
talks about integrating the two,

00:20:11.231 --> 00:20:12.880
but we said, "How do you do those

00:20:12.881 --> 00:20:15.105
need assessment and
solution matching? "

00:20:15.106 --> 00:20:19.990
That's when we realize
that Microsoft also has,

00:20:19.991 --> 00:20:24.220
specifically MSR has
this Karya, along with Karya,

00:20:24.221 --> 00:20:26.125
it has Sangam, Lynda,

00:20:26.126 --> 00:20:28.615
a part of Linkedin for
skill development.

00:20:28.616 --> 00:20:31.645
All this came to our notice.

00:20:31.646 --> 00:20:33.300
So, we're very
interested in seeing

00:20:33.301 --> 00:20:35.110
how to tighten
this collaboration at

00:20:35.111 --> 00:20:38.460
this of point of time.

00:20:38.461 --> 00:20:41.100
But more specifically,
let's understand

00:20:41.101 --> 00:20:44.455
this need assessment
and interest matching.

00:20:44.456 --> 00:20:46.660
So, most of the solutions that

00:20:46.661 --> 00:20:49.120
exist are pushed down, top down.

00:20:49.121 --> 00:20:51.085
So, you push
a problem definition,

00:20:51.086 --> 00:20:52.900
and then you expect that people

00:20:52.901 --> 00:20:55.020
upgrade their skills to match it,

00:20:55.021 --> 00:20:56.590
to solve the problems.

00:20:56.591 --> 00:20:58.320
However, we realize
that there is lack

00:20:58.321 --> 00:20:59.740
of skilling and there's more

00:20:59.741 --> 00:21:03.265
seriously a lack of interest
assessment of the people.

00:21:03.266 --> 00:21:05.485
Are all field trips,
and in fact we're

00:21:05.486 --> 00:21:07.500
quite amazed to see

00:21:07.501 --> 00:21:09.240
the amount of work
that already exists,

00:21:09.241 --> 00:21:11.750
not only across the globe,

00:21:11.751 --> 00:21:13.420
but especially to India,

00:21:13.421 --> 00:21:16.995
to very nicely categorize
a people's interests.

00:21:16.996 --> 00:21:19.520
So, how do we boost
people's self-confidence?

00:21:19.521 --> 00:21:22.540
By reinforcing their skill,

00:21:22.541 --> 00:21:24.880
their interests, and also,

00:21:24.881 --> 00:21:27.385
we need to create this
strong connectivity industry

00:21:27.386 --> 00:21:29.260
that is the forward linkage part,

00:21:29.261 --> 00:21:31.270
which is concerned
with placement,

00:21:31.271 --> 00:21:34.200
and the backward linkage,
their interest.

00:21:34.201 --> 00:21:38.545
Okay. So, we started with
lots of field trips,

00:21:38.546 --> 00:21:40.000
village youth interaction,

00:21:40.001 --> 00:21:41.895
self-help group
member interactions.

00:21:41.896 --> 00:21:44.140
Especially we took up bonds.

00:21:44.141 --> 00:21:46.205
A bond is a specific task,
which is of tailoring.

00:21:46.206 --> 00:21:48.710
How do you upgrade
the skill levels of tailoring?

00:21:48.711 --> 00:21:52.685
We're quite aghast to see
that in the rural sector,

00:21:52.686 --> 00:21:54.570
there's lot of talent,

00:21:54.571 --> 00:21:57.145
but there's really
no standardization.

00:21:57.146 --> 00:22:00.910
So, if there was a big industry
in the area we walked in,

00:22:00.911 --> 00:22:02.800
they wanted close to 10,000

00:22:02.801 --> 00:22:04.800
uniform stitched over
a period of one month,

00:22:04.801 --> 00:22:07.710
and then [inaudible] put
a ban on plastic bags.

00:22:07.711 --> 00:22:10.480
&gt;&gt; There was a demand, high
demand for [inaudible] bags.

00:22:10.481 --> 00:22:11.740
But absolutely, it was so

00:22:11.741 --> 00:22:13.450
difficult to enforce
standardization.

00:22:13.451 --> 00:22:15.095
That's when we realized
skill development

00:22:15.096 --> 00:22:16.660
and need assessment needs

00:22:16.661 --> 00:22:18.840
to be brought together
very closely.

00:22:18.841 --> 00:22:20.980
There's also led
us to interaction

00:22:20.981 --> 00:22:22.525
with regionals or
college students,

00:22:22.526 --> 00:22:25.870
and NSDC Skilling
Center Students.

00:22:27.330 --> 00:22:29.875
Interestingly, we realized that

00:22:29.876 --> 00:22:31.540
national and
international standards

00:22:31.541 --> 00:22:32.820
can all be leveraged.

00:22:32.821 --> 00:22:34.830
So, the idea was to interact

00:22:34.831 --> 00:22:36.790
locally and scale up nationally,

00:22:36.791 --> 00:22:37.925
so the local interaction,

00:22:37.926 --> 00:22:41.260
we put in the numbers here,
they may appear to be small,

00:22:41.261 --> 00:22:43.140
but that's absolutely
critical for us to

00:22:43.141 --> 00:22:45.975
understand, the
qualitative insights.

00:22:45.976 --> 00:22:49.495
However, as you see in
the next part, here,

00:22:49.496 --> 00:22:52.255
we also leverage
existing national work,

00:22:52.256 --> 00:22:55.720
for example, National Career
Service government of India,

00:22:55.721 --> 00:22:57.850
it has registered a large number

00:22:57.851 --> 00:23:01.100
of job seekers, 42 million,

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:04.610
2015 National
Classification Occupations,

00:23:04.611 --> 00:23:06.855
and the number of
listed occupations are

00:23:06.856 --> 00:23:09.535
close to 3,000, which
is again large.

00:23:09.536 --> 00:23:11.590
Then, the government of India

00:23:11.591 --> 00:23:13.775
also refers to Personality Tests,

00:23:13.776 --> 00:23:15.970
which have been pretty
much standardized

00:23:15.971 --> 00:23:19.150
and some of them are also
part of IBM Watson for,

00:23:19.151 --> 00:23:21.540
if you're informed and tried it.

00:23:21.541 --> 00:23:26.755
I think MBD is part of
IBM Watson, and so on.

00:23:26.756 --> 00:23:29.740
So, at this point, I'll run you

00:23:29.741 --> 00:23:32.270
through a demo of
the entire system,

00:23:32.271 --> 00:23:34.035
so I request approval to come.

00:23:34.036 --> 00:23:36.010
&gt;&gt; So, basically we have

00:23:36.011 --> 00:23:38.225
thought of Loka Udyog
in four parts.

00:23:38.226 --> 00:23:40.395
First is the Aspiration Finder,

00:23:40.396 --> 00:23:42.985
because we found
that in rural areas,

00:23:42.986 --> 00:23:44.890
we are targeting
rural youth here.

00:23:44.891 --> 00:23:46.540
So, in rural areas,

00:23:46.541 --> 00:23:49.585
people are not aware of
what they can aspire for.

00:23:49.586 --> 00:23:52.155
So, there is a serious lack
of aspirations.

00:23:52.156 --> 00:23:54.555
So, that is one platform
which we are developing,

00:23:54.556 --> 00:23:56.605
it is called
the Aspiration Finder.

00:23:56.606 --> 00:23:59.330
Where we'll lure the user
through a series

00:23:59.331 --> 00:24:02.375
of steps starting from
the Personality Test first,

00:24:02.376 --> 00:24:04.155
because these rural youth,

00:24:04.156 --> 00:24:06.885
they do not know what kind
of personality they have.

00:24:06.886 --> 00:24:09.920
So, we will be having
first, a personality test,

00:24:09.921 --> 00:24:14.800
followed by leading them to
different career options,

00:24:14.801 --> 00:24:16.720
which they will select from

00:24:16.721 --> 00:24:18.270
a series of metrics and this is

00:24:18.271 --> 00:24:21.585
based on national and
international codes,

00:24:21.586 --> 00:24:22.830
like if you see here,

00:24:22.831 --> 00:24:24.450
the second step is knowing

00:24:24.451 --> 00:24:27.610
your career aspirations,
I'll just move ahead.

00:24:27.611 --> 00:24:30.490
Yeah. So, through

00:24:30.491 --> 00:24:33.925
a very simple questionnaire
using graphical format,

00:24:33.926 --> 00:24:37.225
we will be asking
the user to answer

00:24:37.226 --> 00:24:39.600
the questions and let him know

00:24:39.601 --> 00:24:42.240
his career or
his personality type,

00:24:42.241 --> 00:24:47.855
and then we will be leading
him to a set of selections,

00:24:47.856 --> 00:24:50.915
which he will base
on his interests.

00:24:50.916 --> 00:24:53.150
So, this entire thing is based on

00:24:53.151 --> 00:24:55.660
the National Glass
classification of occupations.

00:24:55.661 --> 00:24:57.395
As you can see,

00:24:57.396 --> 00:25:01.435
there is this four digit
code which appears,

00:25:01.436 --> 00:25:05.595
and these are national as
well as international codes.

00:25:05.596 --> 00:25:07.990
So, basically
the person will be able

00:25:07.991 --> 00:25:10.260
to find out where he can fit in.

00:25:10.261 --> 00:25:14.025
What kind of occupation will
he be interested in further?

00:25:14.026 --> 00:25:15.860
Because what happens
is these youth,

00:25:15.861 --> 00:25:17.715
they do not have any knowledge of

00:25:17.716 --> 00:25:19.080
what kinds of occupations

00:25:19.081 --> 00:25:20.875
their skills can be
translated into.

00:25:20.876 --> 00:25:25.680
For example, a person might
be physically very fit,

00:25:25.681 --> 00:25:29.410
but he might know how we can
leverage this skill of his.

00:25:29.411 --> 00:25:32.455
So, he could very well be
a very good police officer.

00:25:32.456 --> 00:25:35.575
So, linking the
person's skills with

00:25:35.576 --> 00:25:37.780
their career options and also

00:25:37.781 --> 00:25:40.330
considering a parameter
of his interest,

00:25:40.331 --> 00:25:41.915
because if there is no interest

00:25:41.916 --> 00:25:43.310
in the job that you are doing,

00:25:43.311 --> 00:25:45.570
you will not get
any satisfaction out of it.

00:25:45.571 --> 00:25:47.440
So, we are just concentrating on

00:25:47.441 --> 00:25:50.150
the Japanese concept of Ikigai,

00:25:50.151 --> 00:25:54.280
which is exploiting
your reason purpose for being.

00:25:54.281 --> 00:25:56.720
So, when we spoke about
this concept to the youth,

00:25:56.721 --> 00:26:01.400
they were very much
interested in it, and then,

00:26:01.401 --> 00:26:07.580
similar to the first choice,

00:26:07.581 --> 00:26:11.305
we will also be giving
him 10 choices mode,

00:26:11.306 --> 00:26:14.380
nine other choices in
all 10 career options,

00:26:14.381 --> 00:26:18.040
which we feel might
be suitable for him.

00:26:18.041 --> 00:26:21.750
But again, just having
the interest is not sufficient,

00:26:21.751 --> 00:26:23.420
there should also be aptitude

00:26:23.421 --> 00:26:26.010
for going for that
particular occupation.

00:26:26.011 --> 00:26:29.080
So, we will be having
some first aptitude tests.

00:26:29.081 --> 00:26:31.085
So, this mapping will be done.

00:26:31.086 --> 00:26:33.190
Key for what kind of occupations,

00:26:33.191 --> 00:26:35.650
what kind of aptitudes
who will require?

00:26:35.651 --> 00:26:44.110
So, yeah.

00:26:44.111 --> 00:26:46.420
So, this is the
Aptitude Test and then,

00:26:46.421 --> 00:26:47.930
it will reel him to

00:26:47.931 --> 00:26:51.070
the final career options
without percentage of matching,

00:26:51.071 --> 00:26:54.555
and then the user will
also be lead their to

00:26:54.556 --> 00:26:57.505
the respective skilling courses

00:26:57.506 --> 00:26:59.855
based on where is
aptitudes are lacking.

00:26:59.856 --> 00:27:01.940
